# Scratch queue rows OXD (plan_process_overhaul.md P2.1). Data: the queue table in scratch_queue.md is generated
# from this file (python3 tools/status_index.py). Format: tools/scratch_query/qrows.py docstring.
# Run: qrun.py run OUT feature_writeup/testing/rows/OXD.qb RES [--section KEY] [--rows ID,...]

@@section 1
@@title SQ-OXD Creative Oxidation P1-P2: core port, state properties, random ticks, 2026-11-25 ([plan_creative_oxidation.md](../plan_creative_oxidation.md) sections 4 and 5, [create_oxidized.md](../create_oxidized.md) OXD-01, OXD-08, OXD-11, OXD-12; TODO `mod-integration #28`)
@@date 2026-11-25
@@jars creativeengineering
@@sources development/creativeEngineering/members/creativeoxidation/src
@@prep toml creativeoxidation-common.toml oxidation speedFactor 100.0
@@text
@@text Creative Engineering 2.0.0 of 2026-11-25 or later (a bundle since then: nests Creative Oxidation, `creativeoxidation`). Fresh worlds only: P2 changes the block state ids of the 45 target blocks. Staged textures come in P6, so these rows read block states, not looks. `speedFactor` 100 in `config/creativeoxidation-common.toml`.
@@table
## SQ-OXD-07 | state properties only on the 45 targets (B1)
@group A
@commands Place iron bars, a glass pane, an oak door, an Andesite Casing, a Fluid Pipe and Create Deco copper bars; test each with `execute if block` on `creativeoxidation_stage`
@pass Boot log has no mixin or tag error naming `creativeoxidation`; Fluid Pipe and Create Deco copper bars match `[creativeoxidation_stage=unaffected,creativeoxidation_waxed=false]`; the other four have no such property (the command errors, no `say` line)
@fails Properties on a non-target: the Registrate pending id leaks (OxidationTargets.takeForStateDefinition); none on the targets: RegistrateBlockBuilderMixin did not apply; a mixin apply error at boot: `createEntry()Lnet/minecraft/world/level/block/Block;` not found (Registrate version) or the refmap missing from the nested jar
bootreject (Mixin apply failed|InvalidInjectionException|InjectionError).*creativeoxidation
bootreject Couldn't load tag creativeoxidation:oxidizable_blocks
> forceload add 0 0 48 16
> setblock 0 100 0 minecraft:iron_bars
> setblock 2 100 0 minecraft:glass_pane
> setblock 4 100 0 minecraft:oak_door[half=lower]
> setblock 6 100 0 create:andesite_casing
> setblock 8 100 0 create:fluid_pipe
> setblock 10 100 0 createdeco:copper_bars
> execute if block 0 100 0 minecraft:iron_bars[creativeoxidation_stage=unaffected] run say oxd07-bad-bars
> execute if block 2 100 0 minecraft:glass_pane[creativeoxidation_stage=unaffected] run say oxd07-bad-pane
> execute if block 4 100 0 minecraft:oak_door[creativeoxidation_stage=unaffected] run say oxd07-bad-door
> execute if block 6 100 0 create:andesite_casing[creativeoxidation_stage=unaffected] run say oxd07-bad-casing
> execute if block 8 100 0 create:fluid_pipe[creativeoxidation_stage=unaffected,creativeoxidation_waxed=false] run say oxd07-pipe-ok
> execute if block 10 100 0 createdeco:copper_bars[creativeoxidation_stage=unaffected,creativeoxidation_waxed=false] run say oxd07-decobars-ok
waitlog oxd07-decobars-ok 20
expect oxd07-pipe-ok
reject oxd07-bad-
## SQ-OXD-01 | aging at speedFactor 100: pipe and casing reach oxidized (OXD-01)
@group A
@commands Fluid Pipe and Copper Casing 12 blocks apart in a force-loaded chunk; `randomTickSpeed` 4096 for 30 s
@pass both report `creativeoxidation_stage=oxidized`
@fails still unaffected: `BlockStateBaseMixin.isRandomlyTicking` not forcing true, the tag not bound, or `enabled` false; partly aged: raise the wait
> forceload add 0 32 16 48
> setblock 0 100 40 create:fluid_pipe
> setblock 12 100 40 create:copper_casing
> gamerule randomTickSpeed 4096
sleep 30
> execute if block 0 100 40 create:fluid_pipe[creativeoxidation_stage=oxidized] run say oxd01-pipe-oxidized
> execute if block 12 100 40 create:copper_casing[creativeoxidation_stage=oxidized] run say oxd01-casing-oxidized
waitlog oxd01-casing-oxidized 20
expect oxd01-pipe-oxidized
> gamerule randomTickSpeed 3
## SQ-OXD-08 | random ticks: waxed and non-targets unchanged, a ticking door still ticks (B2)
@group A
@commands As SQ-OXD-01 with a waxed Fluid Pipe and a plain Mechanical Pump next to an aging pipe; a mod door or pane that random ticks on its own
@pass waxed pipe stays `unaffected,waxed=true`; the aging pipe moves on; a block that random ticks by itself keeps doing so
@fails waxed pipe aged: `OxidationRules.isAging` ignores wax; the self-ticking block stopped: isRandomlyTicking forced false (B2 not fixed)
> forceload add 0 64 16 80
> setblock 0 100 72 create:fluid_pipe[creativeoxidation_waxed=true]
> setblock 12 100 72 create:fluid_pipe
> gamerule randomTickSpeed 4096
sleep 30
> execute if block 0 100 72 create:fluid_pipe[creativeoxidation_stage=unaffected,creativeoxidation_waxed=true] run say oxd08-waxed-unchanged
> execute if block 12 100 72 create:fluid_pipe[creativeoxidation_stage=oxidized] run say oxd08-aging-oxidized
waitlog oxd08-aging-oxidized 20
expect oxd08-waxed-unchanged
> gamerule randomTickSpeed 3
look a block that random ticks on its own and carries the properties: none among the 45 targets is known; check that no target lost behavior it had (copper door, ladder, scaffolding)
## SQ-OXD-11 | contraption and schematic keep stages (OXD-11)
@group A
@commands A weathered Fluid Tank moved on a contraption; a schematic of waxed pipes printed by a Schematicannon
@pass the stage and wax are kept after assembly, disassembly and printing
@fails stage lost: Create copies only the block state it reads; to P5 with the B4 conversions
@draft contraption assembly and Schematicannon printing need a client or a scripted structure; owner LOOK until a driver step exists
## SQ-OXD-15 | dedicated server and client join, no state mismatch (OXD-12)
@group A
@commands Dedicated server with the bundle, client joins, places a Fluid Pipe and ages it with the debug stick
@pass no disconnect for a block state mismatch; the client shows the pipe; F3 shows the two properties on the client
@fails disconnect: client jar differs from the server's (both must carry the member)
@client true
@draft needs a client join on the scratch server

@@section 2
@@title SQ-OXD Creative Oxidation P3-P4: staged items, drops, placing, names, waxing, scraping, lightning, soap, 2026-11-25 ([plan_creative_oxidation.md](../plan_creative_oxidation.md) sections 4 and 5, [create_oxidized.md](../create_oxidized.md) OXD-02 to OXD-06; TODO `mod-integration #31`)
@@date 2026-11-25
@@jars creativeengineering
@@sources development/creativeEngineering/members/creativeoxidation/src
@@text
@@text Creative Engineering 2.0.0 of 2026-11-25 or later with Creative Oxidation P3-P4 (`creativeoxidation` 1.0.0-ce-19.2-02 nested). Fresh worlds only (P2 state ids). Staged textures come in P6, so these rows read block states and item NBT (`CreativeOxidationStage`, `CreativeOxidationWaxed`), not looks. Default `config/creativeoxidation-common.toml` (`keepStageOnBreak` true) unless a row edits it.
@@table
## SQ-OXD-02 | honeycomb wax; waxed block does not age (OXD-02)
@group A
@commands Fluid Pipe; `cdevtest use` with 2 honeycomb; a second use on the waxed pipe; `randomTickSpeed` 4096 for 30 s next to an unwaxed control pipe
@pass first use: `waxed=true`, one honeycomb left; second use: not consumed, still one honeycomb; after 30 s the waxed pipe is still `unaffected,waxed=true` and the control pipe is `oxidized`
@fails not waxed: OxidationEvents.onRightClickBlock not registered (CreativeOxidation constructor) or the tag not bound; honeycomb not used up: `instabuild` read wrong; waxed pipe aged: OxidationRules.isAging ignores wax
> forceload add 0 96 16 112
> setblock 0 100 100 create:fluid_pipe
> setblock 12 100 100 create:fluid_pipe
> cdevtest use 0 100 100 held=minecraft:honeycomb*2
> execute if block 0 100 100 create:fluid_pipe[creativeoxidation_stage=unaffected,creativeoxidation_waxed=true] run say oxd02-waxed
waitlog oxd02-waxed 10
expect verb=use .*main=minecraft:honeycomb\*1\b
> cdevtest use 0 100 100 held=minecraft:honeycomb*1
expect verb=use who=fake hand=main action=block result=PASS
> gamerule randomTickSpeed 4096
sleep 30
> gamerule randomTickSpeed 3
> execute if block 0 100 100 create:fluid_pipe[creativeoxidation_stage=unaffected,creativeoxidation_waxed=true] run say oxd02-waxed-unchanged
> execute if block 12 100 100 create:fluid_pipe[creativeoxidation_stage=oxidized] run say oxd02-control-oxidized
waitlog oxd02-control-oxidized 20
expect oxd02-waxed-unchanged
## SQ-OXD-03 | axe and steel wool scrape: wax off, then one stage; durability (OXD-03)
@group A
@commands Waxed weathered Fluid Pipe: `cdevtest use` twice with an iron axe; oxidized Fluid Pipe: once with Immersive Weathering steel wool; a plain pipe with the axe
@pass axe 1: `weathered,waxed=false`, axe `Damage:1`; axe 2: `exposed`, `Damage:2`; steel wool: `oxidized` -> `weathered`, wool `Damage:1`; plain pipe: result PASS, axe undamaged
@fails nothing scraped: OxidationEvents.toolOf (axe by ToolActions.AXE_SCRAPE, steel wool by id `immersive_weathering:steel_wool`); two steps in one click: wax and stage both taken (OxidationManager.scrape); no damage: hurtAndBreak skipped
> forceload add 0 96 16 112
> setblock 0 100 104 create:fluid_pipe[creativeoxidation_stage=weathered,creativeoxidation_waxed=true]
> cdevtest use 0 100 104 held=minecraft:iron_axe
expect verb=use .*main=minecraft:iron_axe\*1\{Damage:1\}
> execute if block 0 100 104 create:fluid_pipe[creativeoxidation_stage=weathered,creativeoxidation_waxed=false] run say oxd03-wax-off
waitlog oxd03-wax-off 10
> cdevtest use 0 100 104 held=minecraft:iron_axe{Damage:1}
expect verb=use .*main=minecraft:iron_axe\*1\{Damage:2\}
> execute if block 0 100 104 create:fluid_pipe[creativeoxidation_stage=exposed,creativeoxidation_waxed=false] run say oxd03-axe-scraped
waitlog oxd03-axe-scraped 10
> setblock 4 100 104 create:fluid_pipe[creativeoxidation_stage=oxidized,creativeoxidation_waxed=false]
> cdevtest use 4 100 104 held=immersive_weathering:steel_wool
expect verb=use .*main=immersive_weathering:steel_wool\*1\{Damage:1\}
> execute if block 4 100 104 create:fluid_pipe[creativeoxidation_stage=weathered,creativeoxidation_waxed=false] run say oxd03-wool-scraped
waitlog oxd03-wool-scraped 10
> setblock 8 100 104 create:fluid_pipe
> cdevtest use 8 100 104 held=minecraft:iron_axe
expect verb=use .*main=minecraft:iron_axe\*1 off=empty state=create:fluid_pipe\[creativeoxidation_stage=unaffected,creativeoxidation_waxed=false
## SQ-OXD-04 | lightning on a rod over oxidized pipes (OXD-04)
@group A
@commands A row of 5 oxidized Fluid Pipes, a lightning rod on the middle one, a waxed oxidized pipe under a second rod; `summon minecraft:lightning_bolt` on each rod; `doFireTick` false
@pass the pipe under the first rod is `unaffected` (the random walks may clean its neighbors a stage or more); the waxed pipe under the second rod stays `oxidized,waxed=true`
@fails nothing cleaned: LightningBoltMixin did not apply (`clearCopperOnLightningStrike` refmap name `m_147150_`) or the bolt struck beside the rod (summon at the rod's top + 1)
