## CQ-OXD-01 | staged textures and partial models render (OXD-07), Design n' Decor blocks included
@group client
@commands Place each of the 34 targets at unaffected, exposed, weathered and oxidized (`setblock ... [creativeoxidation_stage=...]`, a row per stage); a Steam Engine on a boiler (gauge), a Portable Fluid Interface, a Fluid Valve; hold the staged items (`/give` with `CreativeOxidationStage`); F3+T once
@pass every staged block shows the matching copper tint on all its copper faces, connected textures (casing, tank, catwalk, sheet metal, scaffolding) stay connected; the boiler gauge, the interface parts and the valve pointer follow the stage; held and inventory icons follow the item's stage; Design n' Decor's Copper Light and Large Copper Chain age; no purple-black anywhere; boot log has no missing texture warning naming `creativeoxidation`
@fails one stage purple-black: a staged PNG missing (oxidizable_textures.txt lists a sprite without its copy) or not stitched (OxidationClient.onTextureStitch); faces unchanged: QuadRemapper did not find the source sprite (manifest entry or UVs); a moving part plain: the staged partial model JSON or its mixin; the chain tiles with a 2 px break between a staged and a plain block (upstream's chain art sits 2 px lower, expected)
@draft needs a client: setblock grid, F3+T, screenshots per stage by the client driver

