@@date 2026-11-25
@@jars creativeengineering creativecompat creativedevtools
@@sources development/creativeEngineering/members/creativeoxidation/src development/creativeCompat/src/main/java/com/SaintAlfonzo/creativecompat/compat/jei/PackIngredientOrder.java development/creativeCompat/src/main/resources/kubejs_startup/creativecompat/func/jei_order.js kubejs/startup_scripts/jei/order.js development/creativeDevtools/src/main/java/com/SaintAlfonzo/creativedevtools/dump/WorldJeiToolPairs.java tools/jei_world/tab_tools.py tools/jei_world/tab_weathering.py tools/jei_world/common.py
@@text
@@text Creative Engineering 2.0.0 of 2026-11-25 or later with Creative Oxidation P8 (`creativeoxidation` 1.0.0-ce-19.2-04 nested), Creative Compat and Creative Devtools of 2026-11-25 or later. The world rows need `/dumpworldjei` (tool_pairs.json gains `creativeoxidation`) and `/cdevgen jei_world` run once after the install, then a restart (the rows are client assets). Every variant is listed in JEI (R16): 7 per target item (exposed, weathered, oxidized, waxed unaffected to waxed oxidized), the plain item once.
@@table
## CQ-OXD-03 | JEI: Waxing and Scraping, Lightning Conversion, Soap Washing rows for staged blocks (P8)
@group client
@commands After `/dumpworldjei` and `/cdevgen jei_world` and a restart: in JEI, show uses (U) of a Weathered Fluid Pipe and a Waxed Exposed Copper Casing; show recipes (R) of an Exposed Fluid Pipe; open the Waxing and Scraping, Lightning Conversion and Soap Washing tabs
@pass Waxing and Scraping: honeycomb rows (each stage -> its waxed form, 4), axe rows and steel wool rows (waxed -> same stage unwaxed, aged -> one stage back, 7 each), the slots cycle every target item with input and output on the same item; Lightning Conversion: 3 rows (exposed, weathered, oxidized -> plain, unwaxed only); Soap Washing: 7 rows (every staged or waxed form -> plain); U on the Weathered Fluid Pipe lists its honeycomb, axe, steel wool, lightning and soap rows and the spout and fan recipes that take it; R on the Exposed Fluid Pipe lists the axe and steel wool rows from weathered and waxed exposed and the spout and fan recipes that make it; names on every slot read "Waxed Exposed Copper Casing" style
@fails no Creative Oxidation rows: tool_pairs.json has no `creativeoxidation` key (WorldJeiToolPairs.creativeOxidation reflection on OxidationJeiData.dump, the log warns `[dumpworldjei] Creative Oxidation`) or generated.json not regenerated; rows show plain items on both sides: the `nbt` on the `stacks` entries lost (WorldRow stacks parse); U or R finds no row: the subtype interpreter is missing (latest.log `[creativeoxidation] JEI subtypes on 32 items`)
@draft needs a client: /dumpworldjei + /cdevgen on the client world, JEI screenshots by the client driver
## CQ-OXD-04 | JEI lists all 7 variants per staged block; plain items at their usual place, variants in the oxidized family in block, stage, waxed order (R16, R17, P8b)
@group client
@commands JEI item list, no search; then search `fluid pipe` and `copper casing`; `[jei] orderReport = true` in the Creative Compat config and rejoin for kubejs/exported/jei_order.json
@pass latest.log `[creativeoxidation] JEI subtypes on 32 items` and `[jei order] definition: 4 types, ...` with no `bad definition`; the plain Fluid Pipe and Copper Casing sit where they sat before (unplaced, Create's own order); right after the Storage Delight family the Oxidized Copper family: per target item, in the plain items' order, Exposed, Weathered, Oxidized, Waxed, Waxed Exposed, Waxed Weathered, Waxed Oxidized, then the next item; the `fluid pipe` search shows 8 stacks (plain + 7); the Creative Oxidation creative tab lists the same 224 stacks
@fails one stack per item: the subtype interpreter did not register (OxidationJEI is a @JeiPlugin; JEI loads it only from the nested jar's annotations); variants next to their plain item: the `nbt` node did not parse (order.js `oxidized_copper`, PackIngredientOrder NbtRule) or the stage keys differ from OxidationItemData; variants out of order: NbtRule picks the entry with the most matching keys, a waxed exposed stack matched `exposed` means the waxed byte did not compare (NumericTag vs boolean)
@draft needs a client: JEI item list screenshots and the order report by the client driver
